# --- OFFICE STUDIO ---

[req.68]
title = "Encrypted agent-native Office Studio with ONLYOFFICE editing"
story = "As a user, I want a first-class document, spreadsheet, presentation, and PDF studio inside Ion, so that I can create, edit, version, and manage office documents with the same identity, encryption, and agent capabilities as every other Ion workflow."
ac_1  = "THE mounted Office Studio SHALL provide real document, spreadsheet, presentation, PDF/form, template, upload, library, editor, version, restore, archive, download and export workflows with accessible responsive states."
ac_2  = "ION is the canonical actor-scoped document manager and storage service; every committed version is encrypted at rest, content-hashed, immutable, bounded and durable across browser and daemon restart."
ac_3  = "A replaceable OfficeEngine contract separates Ion from ONLYOFFICE-specific editor configuration, health, force-save, disconnect, conversion and compatibility behavior."
ac_4  = "Browser operations require the authenticated Ion actor, exact origin and CSRF for mutations; engine configurations, callbacks, downloads and commands use short-lived scoped tokens and validated JWTs without exposing shared secrets."
ac_5  = "Save callbacks are bounded, authenticated, idempotent and restart-safe; Ion validates and durably commits a downloaded version before acknowledging success, and duplicate, stale, uncertain or failed saves remain honest."
ac_6  = "Imports and exports validate supported extensions, MIME signatures, OOXML archive structure, decompression bounds, macros, embedded content and maximum sizes; macro-enabled or dangerous documents are quarantined or opened read-only."
ac_7  = "Agent office operations preserve the same Ion identity, memory, task, approval, evidence and artifact boundaries; selected content is sent only by explicit user action and proposed document mutations remain reviewable."
ac_8  = "THE editor is mounted through a same-origin WebSocket-capable proxy or another explicitly configured secure origin; direct unauthenticated document-server exposure and arbitrary proxy targets are prohibited."
ac_9  = "COMPOSE, Kubernetes and Helm packaging use a pinned configurable ONLYOFFICE image, while Railway packages that pinned engine inside the single Ion appliance service; every target uses sealed JWT authentication, non-public engine access, health checks, durable canonical Ion versions, graceful save/disconnect behavior and documented resource requirements."
ac_10 = "COMMUNITY branding, AGPL obligations, connection limits and unavailable commercial features remain visible; the domain must support later Developer or hosted engines without data migration."
ac_11 = "PRODUCTION acceptance covers real DOCX, XLSX, PPTX and PDF journeys, JWT/origin/CSRF denial, cross-actor isolation, callback replay, restart, WebSocket reconnect, malicious files, version restore, backup, export and artifact verification."
ac_12 = "NO Office task is marked complete from source presence, an iframe rendering, HTTP 200, simulated callbacks, screenshots or model claims."

